   "flags": [],
   "use": "Among friends, the get-to-know-you question is kodomo iru? (got kids?), answered un, hitori iru. Politely you ask okosan imasu ka? (or okosan wa irasshaimasu ka?), answered futari imasu. The number goes after the noun: kodomo futari iru (I have two kids). kyoudai iru? and kanojo iru? work the same way.",
   "notes": "kodomo dekita = we're having a baby, or we've had kids (kekkon shite kodomo mo dekita). The birth itself is kodomo ga umareru: kodomo umareta (the baby's here).",
   "example": {
    "romaji": "uchi wa kodomo futari iru n da.",
    "ja": "うちは子供二人いるんだ。",
    "english": "We've got two kids."
   },
   "examplePolite": {
    "romaji": "uchi wa kodomo ga futari iru n desu.",
    "ja": "うちは子供が二人いるんです。",
    "english": "We have two children."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "c-kodomo-ga-umareru",
   "romaji": "kodomo ga umareru",
   "polite": "kodomo ga umaremasu",
   "english": "have a baby",
   "ja": "子供が生まれる",
   "kana": "こどもがうまれる",
