   "noun": "kodomo",
   "particle": "ga",
   "verb": "umareru",
   "verbJa": "生まれる",
   "verbSense": "be born",
   "englishVerb": "have",
   "trap": "English 'we had a baby' leads to kodomo ga atta, which isn't said. kodomo o motsu is real but means being a parent as a stage of life (kodomo o motte kara = since I became a parent). Birth news makes the baby the subject: kodomo ga umareta. kodomo o umu (give birth) is said about the mother.",
   "partners": [
    "akachan (baby)",
    "mago (grandchild)",
    "koneko (kittens)"
   ],
   "flags": [],
   "use": "The way to share baby news, with the child as subject: kodomo ga umareta (we had a baby), raigetsu umareru n da (it's due next month). akachan works the same way, and kodomo dekita is the earlier 'we're expecting'.",
   "notes": "Your own birth takes the same verb: toukyou de umareta (I was born in Tokyo).",
