   "flags": [],
   "use": "Used about parenting as a whole: hitori de kodomo o sodateta (she raised her kids alone), kodomo sodateru no tte taihen da yo. Everyday talk often uses the noun kosodate (parenting) instead: ima kosodate-chuu (I'm busy raising kids).",
   "notes": "sodatsu is the intransitive side: inaka de sodatta (I grew up in the countryside). Having a dog is inu o kau; inu o sodateru is only raising one from a puppy.",
