   "flags": [],
   "use": "Used for looking after kids, pets, juniors or ageing parents; o is often dropped in speech: kodomo no mendou mite kureru? (can you watch the kids?). Most often heard with te kureru or te ageru: zutto mendou mite kureta (they always looked out for me).",
   "notes": "mendoumi ga ii = good at looking after people, a common compliment for a senpai or big sister. sewa o suru (kodomo no sewa) is the near twin; mendou o miru adds taking responsibility for someone. It shares the noun with mendokusai (what a hassle) but not the feel.",
   "example": {
    "romaji": "kodomo no mendou mite kureru?",
